{"book":5,"chapter":2,"context":{"chapter":2,"title":"Passing Kin, Defeating Sihon","summary":"Israel passes Edom, Moab and Ammon without fighting, because God had given those lands to Esau's and Lot's descendants, and then defeats Sihon, the Amorite king of Heshbon.","background":"Edom descended from Esau, Jacob's brother; Moab and Ammon from Lot, Abraham's nephew. The bracketed notes about earlier peoples such as the Emims and Horims (vv. 10–12, 20–23) show that other nations had also replaced former inhabitants, under God's rule. The brook Zered and the river Arnon were valleys that marked Moab's borders; Sihon ruled north of the Arnon.","customs":[{"term":"Utterly destroyed","verses":"2:34-35","note":"The Hebrew word (herem) means devoting a city wholly to God in war, so it could not be kept for ordinary gain. Here the livestock and goods were kept as plunder; at Jericho even those were devoted. Readers have long wrestled with these passages."}],"watchFor":["Three times God tells Israel to leave a related nation alone (vv. 5, 9, 19).","The whole fighting generation dies before the next advance (vv. 14–16).","Israel first offers Sihon peaceful passage (vv. 26–29)."],"connections":["Genesis 36:8","Genesis 19:36-38","Numbers 20:14-21","Numbers 21:21-31"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַנֵּפֶן","vanefen","H6437","Hc/Vqw1cp","and we turned"],["וַנִּסַּע","vanisa'","H5265","Hc/Vqw1cp","and we set out"],["הַמִּדְבָּרָה","hamidbarah","H4057","HTd/Ncmsa/Sd","the wilderness towards"],["דֶּרֶךְ","derekh","H1870","HNcbsc","[the] way of"],["יַם","yam-","H3220","HNcmsc","[the] sea of"],["סוּף","suf","H5488","HNtmsa","reed[s]"],["כַּאֲשֶׁר","ka'asher","H834","HR/Tr","just as"],["דִּבֶּר","diber","H1696","HVpp3ms","he had spoken"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["אֵלָי","'elai","H413","HR/Sp1bs","to me"],["וַנָּסָב","vanasov","H5437","Hc/Vqw1cp","and we went around"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["הַר","har-","H2022","HNcmsc","[the] hill country of"],["שֵׂעִיר","s