ends along the west coast of Arabia for about 1,400 miles, and separates Asia from Africa. It is connected with the Indian Ocean, of which it is an arm, by the Strait of Bab-el-Mandeb.","verses":26,"v":[1]},{"id":"seir_1042","name":"Seir","kind":"Region","lat":30.73469,"lon":35.60625,"summary":"The name of a mountainous region occupied by the Edomites, extending along the eastern side of the Arabah from the south-eastern extremity of the Dead Sea to near the Akabah, or the eastern branch of the Red Sea.","verses":24,"v":[4,8,12,22,29]},{"id":"arabah_79","name":"Arabah","kind":"","lat":32.02968,"lon":35.52099,"summary":"Plain, in the Revised Version of 2 Kings 14:25; Josh. 3:16; 8:14; 2 Sam. 2:29; 4:7 (in all these passages the A.V. has “plain”); Amos 6:14 (A.V. “wilderness”).","verses":15,"v":[8]},{"id":"elath_366","name":"Elath","kind":"City","lat":29.5285,"lon":35.00573,"summary":"Grove; trees, (Deut. 2:8), also in plural form Eloth (1 Kings 9:26, etc.); called by the Greeks and Romans Elana; a city of Idumea, on the east, i.e., the Elanitic, gulf, or the Gulf of Akabah, of the Red Sea.","verses":3,"v":[8]},{"id":"ezion-geber_423","name":"Ezion-geber","kind":"City","lat":29.53068,"lon":35.0,"summary":"The giant’s backbone (so called from the head of a mountain which runs out into the sea), an ancient city and harbour at the north-east end of the Elanitic branch of the Red Sea, the Gulf of Akabah, near Elath or Eloth (Num. 33:35; Deut. 2:8).","verses":7,"v":[8]},{"id":"moab_815","name":"Moab","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":31.49916,"lon":35.78051,"summary":"The land of Moab (Jer. 48:24), called also the “country of Moab” (Ruth 1:2, 6; 2:6), on the east of Jordan and the Dead Sea, and south of the Arnon (Num. 21:13, 26).","verses":148,"v":[8,9,18]},{"id":"ar_77","name":"Ar","kind":"","lat":31.44981,"lon":35.59396,"summary":"","verses":6,"v":[9,18,29]},{"id":"zered_1253","name":"Zered","kind":"Water","lat":30.88413,"lon":35.89763,"summary":"Zared, luxuriance; willow bush, a brook or valley communicating with the Dead Sea near its southern extremity (Num. 21:12; Deut. 2:14). It is called the “brook of the willows” (Isa. 15:7) and the “river of the wilderness” (Amos 6:14).","verses":2,"v":[13,14]},{"id":"kadesh-barnea_663","name":"Kadesh-barnea","kind":"Oasis","lat":30.64805,"lon":34.42261,"summary":"Holy, or Kadesh-Barnea, sacred desert of wandering, a place on the south-eastern border of Palestine, about 165 miles from Horeb. It lay in the “wilderness” or “desert of Zin” (Gen. 14:7; Num. 13:3-26; 14:29-33; 20:1; 27:14), on the border of Edom (20:16).","verses":10,"v":[14]},{"id":"ammon_58","name":"Ammon","kind":"","lat":31.95522,"lon":35.94503,"summary":"The usual name of the descendants of Ammon, the son of Lot (Gen. 19:38). From the very beginning (Deut. 2:16-20) of their history till they are lost sight of (Judg. 5:2), this tribe is closely associated with the Moabites (Judg. 10:11; 2 Chr. 20:1; Zeph. 2:8).","verses":12,"v":[19,37]},{"id":"caphtor_275","name":"Caphtor","kind":"","lat":35.17124,"lon":25.0072,"summary":"A chaplet, the original seat of the Philistines (Deut. 2:23; Jer. 47:4; Amos 9:7). The name is found written in hieroglyphics in the temple of Kom Ombos in Upper Egypt.","verses":3,"v":[23]},{"id":"heshbon_565","name":"Heshbon","kind":"City","lat":31.79819,"lon":35.80986,"summary":"Intelligence, a city ruled over by Sihon, king of the Amorites (Josh. 3:10; 13:17). It was taken by Moses (Num. 21:23-26), and became afterwards a Levitical city (Josh. 21:39) in the tribe of Reuben (Num. 32:37).","verses":37,"v":[24,26,30]},{"id":"river_of_arnon_1225","name":"river of Arnon","kind":"Water (River)","lat":31.4288,"lon":35.67701,"summary":"Swift, the southern boundary of the territory of Israel beyond Jordan, separating it from the land of Moab (Deut. 3:8, 16). This river (referred to twenty-four times in the Bible) rises in the mountains of Gilead, and after a circuitous course of about 80 miles through a deep ravine it falls into the Dead Sea nearly opposite Engedi.","verses":11,"v":[24,36]},{"id":"kedemoth_675","name":"Kedemoth","kind":"City","lat":31.64607,"lon":35.89454,"summary":"Beginnings; easternmost, a city of Reuben, assigned to the Levites of the family of Merari (Josh. 13:18).","verses":4,"v":[26]},{"id":"jordan_653","name":"Jordan","kind":"Water (River)","lat":33.18645,"lon":35.61916,"summary":"But besides these two historical fountains there is a third, called the Hasbany, which rises in the bottom of a valley at the western base of Hermon, 12 miles north of Tell-el-Kady.","verses":177,"v":[29]},{"id":"jahaz_617","name":"Jahaz","kind":"City","lat":31.501,"lon":35.92063,"summary":"Trodden down (called also Jahaza, Josh. 13:18; Jahazah, 21:36; Jahzah, 1 Chr. 6:78), a town where Sihon was defeated, in the borders of Moab and in the land of the Ammonites beyond Jordan, and north of the river Arnon (Num. 21:23; Deut. 2:32).","verses":5,"v":[32]},{"id":"aroer_93","name":"Aroer","kind":"City","lat":31.47151,"lon":35.82192,"summary":"A town on the north bank of the Arnon (Deut. 4:48; Judg. 11:26; 2 Kings 10:33), the southern boundary of the kingdom of Sihon (Josh. 12:2).","verses":9,"v":[36]},{"id":"gilead_475","name":"Gilead","kind":"Region","lat":32.75,"lon":35.75,"summary":"Hill of testimony, (Gen. 31:21), a mountainous region east of Jordan. From its mountainous character it is called “the mount of Gilead” (Gen. 31:25).","verses":80,"v":[36]},{"id":"jabbok_609","name":"Jabbok","kind":"Water (River)","lat":32.19324,"lon":35.6763,"summary":"A pouring out, or a wrestling, one of the streams on the east of Jordan, into which it falls about midway between the Sea of Galilee and the Dead Sea, or about 45 miles below the Sea of Galilee.","verses":7,"v":[37]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[6437,6437,6437,6437,5265,5265,4057,4057,4057,1870,1870,5488,5488,5488,3220,834,3068,3068,1696,1696,1696,7227,7227,7227,3117,5437,5437,5437,20